OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Coal Board and the miners' union
OL,6, plan to meet on Sunday night.
OL,7,F
OL,8,FThe new talks were agreed after the
OL,9,FCoal Board wrote to the NUM offering to
OL,10,Fre-open negotiations.
OL,11,F
OL,12,FThe Board's letter apparently refers to
OL,13,Fthe question of whether uneconomic pits
OL,14,Fshould be closed.
OL,16,FIn its reply the NUM says it hopes the
OL,17,Fmeeting will take place - but Mr
OL,18,FScargill has said there is no change in
OL,19,Fthe union's position.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18103
SC,0003
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G3/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Trades Union Conference voted today
OL,6, not to boycott the National Economic
OL,7, Development Council.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FMr David Basnett, chairman of the TUC
OL,10,FEconomic Committee, in opposing a move
OL,11,Fto pull out of the NEDC, said it was
OL,12,Fnecessary to fight against monetarism
OL,13,Fusing any means possible.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FCongress also approved unanimously a
OL,16,Fmotion condemning the Government's
OL,17,F"damaging" education policy.
OL,18,F
OL,19,FProposed tax reforms were criticised
OL,20,Fand a "fair and equitable system of
OL,21,Fpersonal income tax" called for.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
SC,0004
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Transport union leaders have called on
OL,6, all dockers still working to withdraw
OL,7, their labour.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FThe TGWU Docks and Waterways Committee
OL,10,Fhas also asked the union executive to
OL,11,Fcall for the "full physical support" of
OL,12,Fother unions.
OL,14,FThe committee condemned the attempt by
OL,15,Fthe Port of London Authority to hold
OL,16,Fits own ballot of dockers at Tilbury.
OL,18,FIt said such a ballot would provide a
OL,19,Fdistorted response and would probably
OL,20,Flead to similar moves by other port
OL,21,Fauthorities.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 05-09-84   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18105
SC,0005
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1788570294
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The talks between British Railways and
OL,6, the two main rail unions have ended
OL,7, inconclusively, but BR hopes that next
OL,8, week's disruption can be averted.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe unions have planned a work-to-rule
OL,11,Ffrom Monday, followed by a 24-hour
OL,12,Fstrike of rail and tube in the London
OL,13,Farea on Wednesday in protest against
OL,14,Fproposed cuts in jobs.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FUnion leaders said the talks had made
OL,17,Fsome progress and British Rail was
OL,18,Fhopeful that services would be normal
OL,19,Fon Monday. The rail unions report to
OL,20,Ftheir executives on Friday and Mr Jimmy
OL,21,FKnapp of the NUR said the situation was
OL,22,F"delicately poised".
OL,23,                      D]CFrom 05-09-84
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18106
