OL,3,T]W-,,%-,,%-,,%S#!!" #!!!#!##!#!
OL,4,Q]             GEXCHANGES Close
OL,5,F
OL,6,FWidespread switching of funds into the
OL,7,Fdollar dragged other major currencies
OL,8,Ftowards all-time lows. Dealers again
OL,9,Fcited US interest rate trends.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FSterling, whose value in Continental
OL,12,Fterms remained unimpaired despite an
OL,13,Fapparent absence of Bank of England
OL,14,Fsupport, plumbed a new low of $1.2805
OL,15,Fbefore closing at $1.2815, for a loss
OL,16,Fof exactly one cent on the day.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe Deutsche Mark, meanwhile, dropped
OL,19,Fto a 13-year low of 2.9550 - and this
OL,20,Fin the face of considerable Bundesbank
OL,21,Fintervention.
OL,22,F
OL,23,Q]GFromC05-09-84G  teletextarchive.com
